# DNS cache admin — API.md §Cache
#
# Entry stages (CONTEXT.md §Cache): fresh (within TTL), stale (past TTL but
# inside the RFC 8767 serve-stale window — outage insurance), expired (dead
# weight awaiting eviction or a clean).

@base = {{host}}

### Usage snapshot: entries by stage, lifetime hit/miss/eviction counters,
### and load_percent = entries / capacity.
GET {{base}}/api/v1/cache
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}

### Remove expired entries now. Stale entries are kept — expect
### removed_stale: 0 here; they are what serve-stale survives an upstream
### outage on.
POST {{base}}/api/v1/cache/clean
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}

### Explicitly purge the stale window too (an admin choice, not the default).
POST {{base}}/api/v1/cache/clean?stale=true
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}

